# Test fixtures are USER-side workspaces: the tests run `nros sync` /
# `nros codegen-system` / cmake inside them, so each one accumulates the same
# three artifact kinds. Several leaves carried their own `/build/` line; the
# rest did not, which is why a fixture sweep leaves a dozen untracked trees
# behind. One rule per kind here instead of one file per fixture.

# cmake / west build trees.
**/build/

# Codegen output. These are generated from the HOST's message packages, so
# they do not exist in a fresh clone and must never be committed — which is
# also why no `Cargo.lock` beside them may be committed (it would name crates
# nobody has). Enforced by `check-leaf-lockfiles`; this keeps them from being
# staged by accident in the first place.
**/generated/

# `nros sync` writes a one-line `include = ["…/nros-patch.toml"]` into each
# leaf `.cargo/`, pointing at a gitignored, host-specific central patch file.
**/.cargo/config.toml

# …except these three, which are hand-authored SOURCE: they select the
# cross-compilation target for a FreeRTOS entry (`[build] target =
# thumbv7m-none-eabi`), not sync output. `nros sync` appends its patch block to
# them, so they show as modified during a run — that is expected, and they stay
# tracked.
!multi_pkg_workspace_freertos/firmware/.cargo/config.toml
!n_board_agnostic_run_plan/freertos_entry/.cargo/config.toml
!orchestration_tiers_freertos/.cargo/config.toml
